      <data key="v_name">wilson2008</data>
      <data key="v_title">Notes 1 I use the term &apos;Norse&apos; throughout: although there were exceptions, most Scandinavian settlers to the Northern Isles came from the region that is now Norway. I also intermittently use the term &apos;Scandinavian&apos; to denote provenance and origins more generally. he periods &apos;Viking Age&apos; (c.AD 800-1100) and &apos;Late Norse&apos; (1100-1300) are referred to as indicators of early or later settlement; otherwise &apos;Norse&apos; is used as a general indicator of the period of Scandinavian occupation on Orkney. he &apos;native&apos; Orcadians of the Late Iron Age encountered by the Norse are also known as the &apos;Picts</data>
